efficacy of a screening protocol using a combination of maternal age plus three biochemical markers--maternal serum     
alpha-fetoprotein (MSAFP), hCG, and unconjugated estriol (E3)--for the antenatal detection of fetal Down syndrome.      
METHODS We conducted a prospective cohort study of 7718 women who underwent the triple-marker analysis between weeks    
