screening. Results: 29 studies INCLUDED, 71 studies EXCLUDED.

### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):
INCLUDED STUDIES (29 total):
- Study 201: CA 125 marker, 29 DS cases, first & second trimester serum study
- Study 203: PAPP-A, free beta-hCG smoking adjustment meta-analysis
- Study 212: Free beta-hCG & PAPP-A first trimester, 22 DS cases
- Study 215: SP1 marker first trimester, 96 DS cases
- Study 217: Weight/ethnic adjustment factors for first trimester markers
- Study 219: PIGF marker first trimester, 45 DS cases
- Study 223: Advanced first trimester screening algorithm (AFS)
- Study 224: PAPP-A, free beta-hCG with NT, 32 DS cases
- Study 225: First trimester maternal serum screening (truncated abstract)
- Study 226: Contingent screening strategies, 32 DS cases
- Study 229: Double test before 10 weeks, 97 DS cases
- Study 231: Finnish first trimester screening, 8 DS cases
- Study 237: ADAM 12 marker first trimester, 28 DS cases
- Study 239: Assisted reproduction first trimester screening
- Study 241: Biochemical screening in assisted reproduction
- Study 252: Nicked free beta-hCG, 6 DS cases (borderline, conservatively included)
- Study 253: Ethnic origin influence on first trimester markers
- Study 260: Free beta-hCG first trimester, 38 DS cases
- Study 261: IVF/ICSI first trimester screening
- Study 262: Predictive modeling from first trimester, 24 DS cases
- Study 271: PSA marker first and second trimester, 102 DS cases
- Study 273: Smoking status correction first trimester, 124 DS cases
- Study 275: IVF placental proteins first trimester
- Study 280: Advanced first trimester algorithm, 81 abnormal karyotypes
- Study 281: PAPP-A, AFP, beta-hCG first trimester, 19 DS cases
- Study 288: SP1 adds little to detection, 15 DS cases
- Study 292: German first trimester screening, 11 DS cases
- Study 293: AFP and free beta-hCG first trimester large population study
- Study 296: S100 protein marker study including first trimester

EXCLUSION CATEGORIES (71 total):
- Second trimester only studies (~35): Triple test, quadruple test, AFP/uE3/hCG at 15-22 weeks
- Ultrasound-only studies (~20): NT, nasal bone, soft markers, Doppler studies
- Review articles (~5): No primary data
- Diagnostic test comparisons (~5): PCR, karyotyping, amniocentesis outcomes
- Other (~6): Policy documents, animal studies (dogs), unclear focus

### 3. Additional context:
Selection criteria applied per protocol:
1. First trimester timing (typically 10-14 weeks gestation)
2. Serum marker component required (PAPP-A, free beta-hCG, or other biochemical markers)
3. Minimum 5 DS cases required per protocol
4. Reference standard must be chromosomal verification or postnatal inspection
5. Study designs: consecutive series, case-control, or randomized trials

Conservative approach: When in doubt, studies were included. Studies combining ultrasound (NT) with serum markers were 
included as they contain relevant serum data. Studies focused solely on ultrasound markers were excluded.

