│ "title": "Ultrasound screening of fetal structural abnormalities at 12 to 14 weeks in Hong Kong", "abstract":        │
│ "OBJECTIVE Ultrasound screening for fetal abnormalities is conventionally performed at 18 to 20 weeks of gestation.  │
│ Recent data suggested that many fetal structural abnormalities could be detected by ultrasound examination at 12 to  │
│ 14 weeks of pregnancy. In this study, we investigated the effectiveness of early ultrasound examination in the       │
