### 3. Additional context:
Key exclusion criteria applied:
1. Studies evaluating second-trimester markers (15-22 weeks) were excluded as the review focuses on first-trimester 
serum tests
2. Ultrasound-only studies (NT, nasal bone, placental volume, etc.) were excluded as they don't evaluate serum markers
3. Studies with fewer than 5 Down's syndrome cases were excluded per protocol
4. Special population studies (IVF, diabetes, twins, haemodialysis) were generally excluded
5. Methodological studies, editorials, and program evaluations were excluded
6. Studies evaluating screening impact/psychosocial outcomes rather than accuracy were excluded

The screening was conservative - when in doubt, studies were included for further review. All decisions include 
individual rationales tied to each study and the protocol requirements.
