│ pregnancies falsely identified as at risk for twins. Our dual marker protocol for mid-trimester pregnancy screening  │
│ combining AFP and free-beta hCG can identify over 77 per cent of twin pregnancies in women less than 35 years of     │
│ age. This benefit may contribute to an improved outcome of pregnancy by early detection of multiple gestation."},    │
│ {"study_index": 598, "title": "Fetal gender impact on multiple‐marker screening results", "abstract": "Maternal      │
