  {"study_index": 304, "title": "Is maternal serum triple screening a better predictor of Down syndrome in female than  
  in male fetuses?", "abstract": "Among euploid gestations, female fetuses have been reported to have significantly     
  lower maternal serum alpha-fetoprotein (MSAFP) and higher human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG) levels than male         
