  among trisomy 21 fetuses detected at amniocentesis after abnormal maternal serum triple screening was compared with   
  that among trisomy 21 fetuses detected at amniocentesis for advanced maternal age (AMA), which served as the control  
  group. Statistical analysis utilized chi-square, Fisher's exact test, and Student's t-test. A P value of less than    
