pregnancies. This assay detected non-specifically all forms of circulating inhibin, dimeric and free alpha subunits, 
whether fully or partially processed. More recently, a new specific assay for dimeric inhibin-A has shown elevated 
results in both a first-trimester and a second-trimester series of cases. In order to assess the value of dimeric 
inhibin-A as a potential marker in the second trimester, we have analysed 157 Down's syndrome cases and used 367 
