routine adjustment of marker levels to allow for them. Moreover, women with positive Down's syndrome screening results  
can be reassured that this is unlikely to be due to them having had assisted reproduction."}, {"study_index": 618,      
"title": "[Screening by maternal serum markers for Down's syndrome]. [Chinese]", "abstract": "OBJECTIVE To investigate  
the optimal method of screening for Down's syndrome (DS) with maternal serum mankers. METHODS Screening by maternal     
serum markers for Down's syndrome was offered to all 2886 pregnant women in Peking Union Medical Hospital during        
1996.11-2001.3. Alpha-fetoprotein (AFP), human chorionic gonadotrophin (free beta-HCG) were used as markers during the  
